;====
:====
# A subtree's theme tags are those turned on nearest it, and in each family its active member is
# the most specific variant of the theme it uses whose tags all hold, or that theme itself. A
# variant of a variant needs the tags of both. Turning a tag off, or using another theme, holds
# for the subtree; a tag set to null is inherited again. A theme a subtree uses by name stays
# active where no variant of it matches.

